 # OrderChaosHNN
-Hamiltonian neural network implementation for Henon Heiles dynamical system learning mix of order and chaos.
 
-This repository contains code that can reproduce the Henon-Heiles system results for [this](https://journals.aps.org/pre/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevE.101.062207) paper.
+Hamiltonian neural network implementation for the Henon-Heiles dynamical system, learning a mix of ordered and chaotic dynamics.
 
+This repository reproduces results from [Phys. Rev. E 101, 062207 (2020)](https://journals.aps.org/pre/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevE.101.062207).
 
-<img src="https://github.com/anshu957/OrderChaosHNN/blob/master/NNSchematic2.png" width="512">
+<img src="NNSchematic2.png" width="512" alt="Hamiltonian neural network schematic">
 
+## Installation
 
+```bash
+pip install torch numpy matplotlib
+```
 
-> NOTE: The code in this repository is inspired and forked from https://github.com/greydanus/hamiltonian-nn
+PyTorch 1.x or 2.x with CPU or CUDA is sufficient.
 
+## Reproducing results
 
+Train a baseline or Hamiltonian neural network on Henon-Heiles trajectories:
+
+```bash
+python main.py --model hamiltonian --epochs 2000
+python main.py --model baseline --epochs 2000
+```
+
+Key arguments: `--hamiltonian` (system Hamiltonian), `--hidden_dim`, `--integrator_scheme` (`RK4`, `RK45`, `Symplectic`), `--activation_fn` (`Tanh`, `ReLU`).
+
+For post-hoc analysis of trained networks and phase-space plots, see [`analyze-henon_heiles.ipynb`](analyze-henon_heiles.ipynb).
+
+Pre-trained network weights are available under [`TrainedNetworks/`](TrainedNetworks/).
+
